# The launcher's Home page: the opening once the start-up disc check is over,
# every button with its description, a status line (a disc verification
# started and canceled), and Play, ending on the game's first scene. Waits on
# each announcement, so a missing or changed line fails the run. Run in
# launcher mode, with accessibility on but muted (as run_level.py runs it):
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py --launcher --muted tools/a11y/launcher_home.drive
# --launcher remembers the disc and turns the update check off, so the
# opening is the same on every run; drive.py refuses to press Choose Disc,
# Discord or the update banner's buttons, which would leave the window.

# The opening waits for the disc check's result and for focus on Play.
wait '"Melee launcher\. Ready to play, Disc not verified\. Play, button\. Start Melee from this disc\. Disc: melee\.iso, Super Smash Bros\. Melee, USA, Revision 2 \(1\.02\)"$'

# Down walks the buttons and wraps to Play.
key Down
wait '"Choose Disc, button\. Pick a Melee disc image: ISO, GCM, CISO, RVZ, GCZ or WIA\."$'
key Down
wait '"Verify Disc, button\. Check the disc image against the original NTSC-U 1\.02 disc\."$'
key Down
wait '"Settings, button\. Graphics, audio, gameplay, controls, online play and the launcher itself\."$'
key Down
wait '"Discord, button\. Join the community Discord server in your browser\."$'
key Down
wait '"Quit, button\. Close Melee PC\."$'
key Down
wait '"Play, button\. Start Melee from this disc\. Disc: melee\.iso, '
key Up
wait '"Quit, button\. '
key Down
wait '"Play, button\. '

# Verify Disc turns into Cancel Verify while the disc is read; the cancel
# comes back in the status line. Hashing the disc takes seconds, so the
# second press lands well before it ends.
key Down Down
wait '"Verify Disc, button\. '
key Return
wait '"Cancel Verify"$'
key Return
wait '"Verify Disc"$'
wait '"Verification canceled\."$' 10

# Play starts the game. With shaders still compiling it says so and starts
# by itself once they are built.
key Up Up
wait '"Play, button\. '
key Return
wait "boot scene: state 0 scene 0$" 120
wait '"Title screen\. Press Start\."$'
